update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5102150Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5207750Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5219167Z ^[[0m
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5219665Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5220306Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5221181Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5221449Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5222112Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5222675Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5222987Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5223553Z    if you are ready to continue.
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5223823Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5224318Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5225071Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5225710Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5226198Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5226355Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5226500Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5226736Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5226929Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5227295Z    can use Nix.
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5227413Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5227511Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5227668Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5227962Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5228418Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5232610Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5232733Z I will:
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5232901Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5233138Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5233718Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5234315Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5234898Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5235284Z  - install Nix in to /nix
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5235664Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5236223Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5236769Z    /root
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5247783Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5248463Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5260265Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5260800Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5261213Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5262660Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5263148Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5282048Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5282845Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5294386Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5295157Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5295743Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5296035Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5296219Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5296517Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5296785Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5297362Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5297694Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5297857Z If you would like to
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5298306Z see the output, try like this:
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5298652Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5298966Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5299494Z   $ sh ./install-nix
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5299698Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5299711Z 
update	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-07T11:59:37.5300000Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
